    "media:imagetext": "- PIEDMONT\nAUTOMATIC\nOXYGEN\nSYSTEM\nThe higher altitudes at which this aircraft operates require prompt\nuse of the automatic oxygen system in case of any sudden change\nin cabin pressure. Should a decompression occur, oxygen masks\nwill drop down automatically. Take\nnearest mask and promptly place\nover nose and mouth and lean back in your seat.\nBRACE\nPOSITIONS\nIn an emergency\nsituation your\nFlight Attendant\nmay request you\nto assume one of\nthe Bracing\nPositions shown.\nINSTRUCTIONS FOR USE OF SEAT BELTS\n, LIFT TO UNFASTEN\nLIFT\nFASTEN\nHold buckle and pull top strap for a tight fit. Please keep your seat\nbelt fastened at all times while in your seat.\nFLOTATION\nCUSHIONS\n1. Lift up at rear\nof cushion\n2. Push down on\nfront to unhook\n3. Use straps\nfor holding\nThe cushion you are seated on will float. In water landing remove\nyour cushion as shown in diagram and take it with you in leaving\nthe aircraft.\nPORTABLE ELECTRONIC DEVICES\nFederal Aviation Agency (FAA) regulation prohibits the operation in-\nflight of certain portable electronic devices since they can interfere\nwith the aircraft's navigation system. Please check with the Flight\nAttendant before operating your radio, dictating machine or recorder.\nPlease Do Not Remove This Card From Aircraft\n0943-00063\n(Rev. 9-15-78)\n2002.121485",
