    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "737\n- PIEDMONT\nIMPORTANT INFORMATION to Our Passengers\nYou are flying aboard a Boeing 73Z, It is unlikely we will encounter\na situ-\n-ation requiring emergency preparations, but it is good practice to be ac\nquainted with the safety features we have provided for you on this aircraft.\nForward\nPassenger\nDoor\nEMERGENCY EXITS\nForward\nService\nDoor\n(Automatic\ninflation\nSlide)\nWINDOW EXITS\n1. To release window\npull down flap,\ngrasp handle and\npull down.\nWindow\nExit\nWindow\nExit\nRear\nPassenger\nDoor\nRear\nService\nDoor\n2. To remove window\n- pull top inward\nand lift up as\nshown.\nFORWARD PASSENGER AND SERVICE DOOR\nTurn handle\ndirection of\narrow.\n2. As hinged\nside moves\nin push other\nside out.\n3. Pull handle\nto inflate\nslide.\n4.\nJump and\nsit in slide.\nPlease Do Not Remove This Card From Aircraft\n0943-00063-09 (Rev. 9-15-78)",
      "- PIEDMONT\nAUTOMATIC\nOXYGEN\nSYSTEM\nThe higher altitudes at which this aircraft operates require prompt\nuse of the automatic oxygen system in case of any sudden change\nin cabin pressure. Should a decompression occur, oxygen masks\nwill drop down automatically. Take\nnearest mask and promptly place\nover nose and mouth and lean back in your seat.\nBRACE\nPOSITIONS\nIn an emergency\nsituation your\nFlight Attendant\nmay request you\nto assume one of\nthe Bracing\nPositions shown.\nINSTRUCTIONS FOR USE OF SEAT BELTS\n, LIFT TO UNFASTEN\nLIFT\nFASTEN\nHold buckle and pull top strap for a tight fit. Please keep your seat\nbelt fastened at all times while in your seat.\nFLOTATION\nCUSHIONS\n1. Lift up at rear\nof cushion\n2. Push down on\nfront to unhook\n3. Use straps\nfor holding\nThe cushion you are seated on will float. In water landing remove\nyour cushion as shown in diagram and take it with you in leaving\nthe aircraft.\nPORTABLE ELECTRONIC DEVICES\nFederal Aviation Agency (FAA) regulation prohibits the operation in-\nflight of certain portable electronic devices since they can interfere\nwith the aircraft's navigation system. Please check with the Flight\nAttendant before operating your radio, dictating machine or recorder.\nPlease Do Not Remove This Card From Aircraft\n0943-00063\n(Rev. 9-15-78)\n2002.121485"
    ],
